  "content": {
    "title": "National Pi Day Food Deals 2026: Score on Pizza, Pies, and Doughnuts",
    "text": "\"Hearst Magazines and Yahoo may earn commission or revenue on some items through these links.\"If you love pie, Pi Day is the perfect excuse to eat more of it than usual. March 14 (aka 3/14) is technically a nod to the mathematical constant pi, which represents the ratio of a circle’s circumference to its diameter. But let's be honest: most people aren't celebrating for the math lesson. They're celebrating for the pie!Here at The Pioneer Woman, we may crack a few Pi Day jokes, but pie itself is serious business. Whether it's a classic apple pie, a rich chocolate pie, or something fun and seasonal like strawberry pie, Ree Drummond knows that a flaky crust filled with something sweet (or even savory) is one of life’s greatest pleasures. (And don't even get us started on pizza pies!) Of course, not everyone feels like baking from scratch—but that’s where Pi Day gets even more fun. Restaurants and pizza chains across the country roll out special deals every March 14, making it easy to celebrate with a slice or two without lifting a rolling pin.No matter how you slice it, Pi Day is the perfect excuse to grab a deal on pizza, dessert pie, or even doughnuts. Some restaurants are offering pies at a festive Pi Day price, while others are slashing costs by 31.4% or handing out free treats with your order. If you're ordering in, dining out, or just treating yourself, these specials make celebrating March 14 extra delicious. Read on to find the best Pi Day food deals this year!7-ElevenIf dinner needs to be quick, 7-Eleven, Speedway, and Stripes are turning Pi Day into a two-day event. On March 13 and 14, 7Rewards and Speedy Rewards members can get any whole pizza for $3.14 in stores or through the 7NOW app. There are also $3.14 quesadillas at Laredo Taco Company, 31.4-cent cinnamon sugar fried pies at Raise the Roost, and $1 7-Select snack pies.Burger KingSweet tooths, rejoice! Royal Perks members can score a free Hershey's Sundae Pie or Cinnamon Apple Pie with a $3.14 purchase on March 14 when ordering through the BK app or online. The pie promo is part of the brand's March 8 through March 14 Perks Week.Blaze PizzaBlaze is keeping its Pi Day tradition alive with another year of cheesy goodness. On March 14, buy one 11-inch pizza at a participating location and get a second 11-inch pizza of equal or lesser value for $3.14 when ordering in person. Guests who stop by on Pi Day will also get a digital code for a later buy-one-get-one-free 11-inch pizza deal in the Blaze app.CrumblCrumbl is getting in on the Pi Day fun with Cookie Dough Pie available through March 14. Then, on Pi Day itself, each store is slated to offer a surprise bonus pie flavor!Pizza HutPizza Hut is rolling out a new Pi Day deal this year: score a $10 large pizza with any three toppings on your choice of Hand-Tossed, Tavern Style, or Thin 'N Crispy crust at participating locations nationwide. It's the perfect way to celebrate 3.14 with friends and family!GoldbellyWant to honor Pi Day with a pie shipped straight to your door? Goldbelly is offering up to 31.4% off select \"regional PIE-cons,\" so you can try famous pies from all over the country at a discount.Grimaldi's PizzeriaFor a simple and delicious way to celebrate, Grimaldi's is selling pizza slices for just $3.14 at select locations on Pi Day.Anthony's Coal Fired Pizza & WingsDine-in guests at ACFP can get a 10-inch coal-fired cheese pizza for $3.14 with the purchase of any beverage on March 14. Hurry in, because the offer is only good until 4 p.m. local time.BJ's Restaurants & BrewhouseIf you love Pizookies, Pi Day is the perfect time to grab one from BJ's. Buy any full-size Pizookie and get a second one for just $3.14. (Just a heads-up: The deal doesn't apply to Pizookie Trios or Party Platters.)DoorDash Pi Day SpecialsOrdering in? DoorDash is featuring Pi Day offers from Pizza Hut, Sbarro, and Blaze Pizza in the app.On March 14, participating Pizza Hut locations are offering buy one medium or large Create Your Own pizza, get one free.Sbarro is offering $4 off eligible $20 orders, or $5 off eligible $25 orders for DashPass members, from March 14 through April 6.Blaze Pizza is also offering a buy-one-get-one-free deal on its 11-inch Simple Pie cheese pizza through April 6.Marco'sMarco's is offering a medium one-topping pizza for $3.14 with the purchase of any large or extra-large menu-priced pizza on March 14 when you use the code PIDAY.Papa JohnsPapa Rewards members can buy any large or XL pizza and get a second one for just $3.14. Plus, starting March 14, members will get access to exclusive deals all week long through March 20.Voodoo DoughnutFor a fun twist on Pi Day, Voodoo Doughnut Fan Club members can get two Banana Cream Pie doughnuts for $3.14.Please note that these deals are subject to availability and may vary by location. It's always a good idea to check with your local restaurant or store to confirm participation. Happy Pi Day!You Might Also Like",
